# SRX400 node 1 (Hub Profile SRX400-1, ISP 1): as-built lab configuration, display set form, generic values.
# Not a Mist render of mist/*.json: lines derived, blocks reordered, lines left out (README); IPv6: paper 9.
# Release: Junos OS Evolved 25.4X300-D30. LAB ONLY: ge-0/0/2 in WAN-VR and the inet.0 default (README, Good to know).
# Replace before use: <hub-MAC>, <mgmt-gateway>, <NODE1-MGMT-IP>, <region> (README, step 2); <cloud>: your Mist cloud;
#   <NTP-SERVER>: the server Mist renders (profiles set pool.ntp.org); <ROOT-PASSWORD-HASH>: set by you or Mist.
set groups wan
set groups lan
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile IOT rule 01 match dynamic-application any
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile IOT rule 01 then routing-instance apbr_OrgOverlay
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile MGMT rule 01 match dynamic-application any
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile MGMT rule 01 then routing-instance apbr_wan
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile CORP rule 01 match dynamic-application any
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile CORP rule 01 then routing-instance apbr_wan
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile GUEST rule 01 match dynamic-application any
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile GUEST rule 01 then routing-instance apbr_wan
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile MEDIA rule 01 match dynamic-application any
set groups apbr security advance-policy-based-routing profile MEDIA rule 01 then routing-instance apbr_wan
